      "message": "feat(mcp): set work offsets, setups, the machine and fixtures\n\nThe MCP server could set stock but not the rest of a setup. Nine new\ntools, each one existing command run through the session History (so\nundo/redo walk them) with every refusal returned as a tool error:\n\n- add_setup / activate_setup (CreateSetup / ActivateSetup)\n- set_wcs (SetWcsOrigin): an absolute origin, or a min/center/max point\n  of the active setup's stock box plus an optional offset - \"G54 off\n  the stock corner\" in one call; an omitted rotation keeps the current\n- set_work_offset (SetSetupWorkOffset): the G54-G59 word a setup posts\n- load_machine (LoadMachine, or SetSetupMachine for one setup): a\n  built-in by name, a .mch file, or clear\n- add_fixture / remove_fixture / move_fixture (TagFixture /\n  UntagFixture / MoveFixture)\n- get_fixture_findings: every setup's fixtures and machine table with\n  their boxes, and each live toolpath collision as data (op, move,\n  struck part, message, blocks_post)\n\nposting::fixture_problems is split into fixture_findings (the hits as\ndata) and the gate's string form, so the tool and the post gate read\none walk; the gate's behaviour is unchanged. The new handlers live in\nmcp/setup_tools.rs and mcp/fixture_tools.rs; tools.rs chains their\ntables rather than growing its own. Pinned by the new mcp_setup suite.\n\nFixes #181\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
